cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use STE-Code in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "STE-Code: Simplified Technical English for Code Documentation"
abstract: >-
  STE-Code adapts the ASD-STE100 Issue 9 aerospace technical writing standard
  (434 pages, 53 rules, 19 categories) into a code documentation domain. It
  provides 6 deployable artifacts including a distilled system prompt,
  self-reading manual, extraction methodology, worked examples, and deployment
  guides. The 5-stage pipeline uses 109 parallel LLM workers for extraction,
  refinement, adaptation, and enrichment.
authors:
